# Keep URLs flat

## Routing model

- CMS pages: single catch-all `src/pages/[...slug].astro`
- Slug is the Orbitype `pages.slug` field — no nested folder per page in `src/pages/`
- Home: slug `"home"` maps to `/` via `localePath()`

## Locale prefixes

- Default locale (`en`): **no prefix** — `/about`, not `/en/about`
- Additional locales: `/<locale>/<slug>` when configured in `src/config/locales.ts`
- Posts: `/posts`, `/posts/[id]/[...slug]` — separate from CMS catch-all

## Do not

- Create `src/pages/about.astro` for CMS content — it bypasses the CMS
- Deeply nest marketing URLs in the filesystem (`/services/consulting/...`) unless slug explicitly contains slashes
- Add trailing-slash redirects without updating sitemap and canonical helpers in `src/lib/seo.ts`

## Static generation

When `RENDER_MODE=static`, `getStaticPaths()` enumerates slugs from Orbitype (or seed). Root path uses `slug: undefined`.

Flat URLs keep Orbitype slugs, sitemap entries, and revalidation paths aligned.
